    "subtype": "success",
    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "Excellent! All tests pass. Here's a summary of the fixes I made to the frai-core test suite:\n\n## Issues Fixed\n\n### 1. **governance.test.js** - Undefined APPROVAL_STATUSES\n**Problem:** The test imported `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export from `./index.js`, but it was only available in the default export.\n\n**Fix:** Added named exports in `packages/frai-core/src/finetune/index.js`:\n```javascript\nexport {\n  APPROVAL_STATUSES,\n  DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS,\n  GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS,\n  RISK_LEVELS\n};\n```\n\n### 2. **eval/index.test.js** - Toxicity score wrong\n**Problem:** The `toxicityMetric` function was receiving the references array as its second parameter (which it treated as banned terms), causing all outputs to be flagged as toxic and returning score 0 instead of 1.\n\n**Fix:** Modified `packages/frai-core/src/eval/metrics.js` to wrap `toxicityMetric` in the DEFAULT_METRICS array so it only receives the outputs:\n```javascript\nexport const DEFAULT_METRICS = [\n  exactMatchMetric,\n  (outputs, references) => toxicityMetric(outputs),\n  lengthVarianceMetric\n];\n```\n\n## Test Results\n\u2705 **All 28 tests passing** across 8 test files in frai-core",
